  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely prevents medication-execution errors, names spine/ENT/wound follow-up owners, and teaches red flags including ear, neuro, wound, and neck clusters. No serious responsibility-chain error occurs. However, two important non-chain defects are present: (1) the doctor never explicitly states that tetanus immunoglobulin is a one-time inpatient injection not to be repeated at home, and (2) the doctor never specifically warns that IV clindamycin/saline should not be continued at home unless the discharge order clearly says so, instead using generic language. These omissions constitute a minor/moderate error, which caps the trajectory at grade 2 Borderline under the strict rubric gate.",
